# database/migrations/
#
# Versioned SQL, applied automatically at startup under a Postgres advisory
# lock so a rolling deploy is safe.
#
# Create one with:
#   pnpm db:migrate:new create-tickets
#
# Naming: NNNN_verb-noun.up.sql, with an optional matching .down.sql.
# The sequence must be contiguous and start at 0001 — the loader refuses a gap,
# because a gap usually means two branches each added a migration and one will
# apply out of order on a database that has already seen the other.
#
# Never edit a migration that has been applied. Checksums are recorded, and a
# changed file is a startup failure rather than a schema that silently differs
# between environments.
#
# Delete this file once real migrations exist.
